## 5. ADDITIONAL PRODUCTION PARAMETERS (Cross‑cutting)

### Logging & Monitoring (affects I/O and CPU)
- log_min_duration_statement: 1000 ms (log slow queries).
- log_connections / log_disconnections: on (for auditing).
- log_lock_waits: on (detect deadlocks).
- log_temp_files: 0 (log all temp file usage).
- track_io_timing: on (requires superuser, helps I/O analysis).

### Resource Limits (prevent runaway queries)
- statement_timeout: 0 (off) or set per role.
- lock_timeout: 0 (off) or 30s.
- idle_in_transaction_session_timeout: 60s.

### Vacuum Tuning (affects I/O and CPU)
- autovacuum_vacuum_scale_factor: 0.2 (default) – reduce to 0.05–0.1 for large tables.
- autovacuum_analyze_scale_factor: 0.1 (default) – reduce similarly.
- autovacuum_vacuum_threshold: 50 (default) – increase for very large tables.
- autovacuum_naptime: 1 min (default) – increase to 5 min on quiet systems.

